@theme startover
// Writer-commons, themes batch. From content/arcs/outlines.md, "The struggle themes". Any department, either shift.
// Fill-ins assumed: {home} a place ("Lisk"), {family} with "my" ("my gran"), {hobby} an activity ("painting"),
// {since} a length of time ("five years"). A beat that names one lists it in needs:, so people without it skip it.

== beat 1
tone: light
hint: Before the Wren? Oh, this and that. You know. Things.
mem: vague
them: Before the Wren? Oh, this and that. Here and there. Very boring. Next question.   [laugh]
them: The Wren's the interesting bit. Ask me about the Wren.
? choice
* All right. What do you like best here?   flavour:listen mem:best
  them: Nobody here knew me before. I like that. I get to be whoever I am now.
* Fair enough. Everyone's got a "this and that".   flavour:share
  them: They do. That's kind of you. Most people push.
them: Next question. Anything but before.

== beat 2
tone: heartfelt
hint: You never pushed about before. I'd like to tell you. If that's all right.
mem: before
them: Before the Wren, I was somebody I didn't like much. Not a bad person. Just not me.   [sigh]
them: Wrong job, wrong place, wrong reasons. I stayed too long because leaving was frightening.
them: Then one day I just signed up. Packed a bag. Walked up the ramp. Never looked back. Well. I look back a bit.
? choice
* That took courage.   flavour:cheer mem:courage
  them: Did it? It felt like running away. Maybe they're the same thing, sometimes.
  + them: Did it? Huh. I've always called it running. I like your word better. I'll use yours.
* I'm glad you came. Whoever you were.   flavour:listen mem:glad
  them: Thank you. That's the nicest thing anyone's said to me in a while.
them: There. That's before. Now you know. I feel lighter.

== beat 3
tone: resolution
hint: I told someone else today. About before. And it was fine.
mem: said
them: I told people. About before. At dinner. Just said it, out loud.
them: Nobody minded. Somebody said, "Same." Somebody else passed the salt.   [laugh]
them: I spent so long hiding it. It was just a story. It's just my story.
? choice
* It's a good story. It ends here.   flavour:listen
  them: It doesn't end. That's the best bit. It just keeps going. Here.
  + them: It ends here and keeps going. With you lot in it. That's the bit I like.
* Pass the salt?   flavour:cheer mem:salt
  them: Ha. Here. That's how this ship says it's all right. Pass the salt.   [laugh]
them: Thanks for being the first one I told. You made it easy.
